# musician: a narrowed loadout for the hyoushigi OODA self-driver.
#
# A musician reuses the broad loadout only by *fork inheritance*; created fresh
# it lands here. The OODA tick runs `kj drive` under THIS loadout, so `drive` is
# the capability that gates self-driving — narrowing the binding now actually
# stops the tick (it didn't before kj grew capability gates).
#
# A player's complete ABC text is prepared for the tick admitted by `kj drive`.
# The runtime validates notation; no model tool call is required. This loadout
# grants `drive` to the tick script and exposes no model-visible tools.
set -e
kj binding allow "drive"
# Deliberately NOT granted: any builtin.* tool instance (block/file/resources/
# kernel_info/tool_search), facade:shell (the safe tool) or facade:shell_write
# (the hot one), facade:submit_input, and fork/drift/transport/operator/admin. A musician
# drives itself and emits ABC text; it does not call tools, fork, merge
# drift, run the transport, or do lifecycle.
